IDs 1..10 are the vanilla sets (`ARTIFACT_SET_VANILLA_*`): names from the old `ArtfsetRepoint` notes in `ArtfsetExpand.cpp`, each ID confirmed from the immediate pushed at each call site. IDs 11..34 are the H5X sets from `artifacts.lua` (`ARTIFACT_SET_HAVEN` … `ARTIFACT_SET_MOON`); the exe never references them.

| ID | Set | `+0x328` call sites (`push <id>` 1 byte before `call`, imm at push+1) | `0x004D8D60` call sites (imm32 `mov edx`) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Dragonish | `0x004BB243`, `0x004BB376`, `0x004BC55D`, `0x00B5053B` | |
| 2 | Dwarven | `0x0097B396`, `0x00B4CD19`, `0x00BC1384` | |
| 3 | Lions | `0x008CF814`, `0x00BBFC09` | |
| 4 | Sar-Issus | `0x004BAB48`, `0x00BBF8EB` | `0x008A3B01` |
| 5 | Necromancers | `0x00C25EBB`, `0x00C262C8` | `0x008A2063`, `0x004E43C6`, `0x00989D0E`, `0x0098A1F2`, `0x009BC586`, `0x008A8160` |
| 6 | Educational | `0x00B4BBF3` | |
| 7 | Hunters | `0x008CE90C` | `0x00A65C38` |
| 8 | Ogres | `0x004BB25F`, `0x004BC579`, `0x008CE937` | |
| 9 | Runic | | `0x004B0E54` |
| 10 | Demonic | `0x008603AD` | |
| 11..34 | H5X sets (`artifacts.lua`) | DLL only — 11 Haven: `ArtfsetHaven.cpp`, 12 Sylvan: `ArtfsetPreserve.cpp` | |

`0x004D8D7F` is the generic call inside `0x004D8D60`.

The commented-out `ArtfsetRepoint_init` patches the immediate byte of each `push`. Its entry `0x008CE933` (Ogres 2*) points at the opcode instead: the immediate is at `0x008CE934`.

## Expansion to 40 sets (`ArtfsetExpand.cpp`)

| Patch | Effect |
|---|---|
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B58C99`, `0x00B5910D` = 40 | Constructors create 40 counts |
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B515ED` = 40 | The equip handler builds 40 counts |
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B5164B` = 40 | The equip handler counts set IDs up to 40 |
| `PATCH_HOOK 0x00B5AD70` (6) → `ArtifactSetCountFork` | Bounds-checked getter: returns 0 when `set_id` is outside the vector, so a 10-entry vector (from an older save, until the next equip change) is never read past its end |

Before this, only the getter's bound was raised (`0x00B5AD7A`). Counts for IDs > 10 were never written, and the getter read past the 10-entry vector.

## Haven set (11) — `ArtfsetHaven.cpp`

| Pieces | Effect | Hook |
|---|---|---|
| 6 | Good morale roll always succeeds and bad morale roll never does (undead are excluded earlier by `has_ability(10)`) | `0x00A6BA30` (good roll `0x00A6BA00`, exit `0x00A6BAF4`) and `0x00A6B920` (bad roll `0x00A6B8F0`, exit `0x00A6B919`) |
| 6 + Haven class | +2 attack and defense per point of positive morale | `0x008A498C` (`func_GetUnitAttack`, `ebx` = attack after the shooter bonuses) and `0x008A23F8` (`func_GetUnitDefense`, `ebx` and `[esp+0x14]` = defense before the defend stance bonus) |

Morale and luck rolls are `CombatUnit` slots `+0x1C8` (bad morale), `+0x1CC` (good morale) and `+0x1D0` (luck); see `h5x-re-combat-unit.mdc`. Supernatural Luck (creature luck wrapper `0x008A3EF0`, own hero skill `0x7C` checked at `0x008A3F98`) is the vanilla model for "always lucky"; the Sylvan set now owns that check (see below).

## Sylvan set (12) — `ArtfsetPreserve.cpp`

"Sylvan hero" = `HERO_CLASS_PRESERVE_MIGHT` (9) / `HERO_CLASS_PRESERVE_MAGIC` (10).

| Pieces | Effect | Hook |
|---|---|---|
| 4 | Hero's effective spellpower ×2 for nature spells (`get_spell_school` = 3) | `0x00BC05A2` (5), end of the CombatHero spellpower-for-spell function: `ebx` = final spellpower before the `>= 1` clamp, `esi` = hero CombatUnit subobject, `edi` = spell ref (0 without spell) |
| 4 + Sylvan class | Sylvan creatures (`get_creature_town` = 4) deal +0.2 damage multiplier to the hero's favored enemies | `PATCH_CALL 0x00A5AE0C` → wrapper calling `FUN_00A59340` then adding the bonus |
| 6 | Creatures always roll good luck | `0x008A3F98` (24) in the creature luck roll `0x008A3EF0`: replaces the own hero skill `0x7C` (Supernatural Luck) check; non-zero → `edi = 1` at `0x008A3FB2` (forced good luck), enemy skill `0xA7` still cancels it. Supersedes the removed `GoldenGoose.cpp` (artifact 161 had this effect) |
| 6 + Sylvan class | Spell damage taken × clamp(1 − luck × DefaultStats `+0x704`, 0, 1) for luck > 0 | `0x0097B055` (17) replaces the skill `0xB3` check; `PATCH_WRTE 0x0097B072` makes it per luck point |

### Sites used by the Sylvan set

- **Spellpower for a spell** (CombatHero, `__thiscall`, `ret 8`): ends at `0x00BC0582`–`0x00BC05B2` (buff `0x14D`, clamp `>= 1`). School dispatch at `0x00BC045E`: `get_spell_school` 1 = dark (`0x00BC04A8`), 2 = light (`0x00BC0473`, `StaffOfTheSaint.cpp`), 3 = nature (no vanilla branch). Also hooked: `ModEffectiveSpellpower.cpp` `0x00BC0582`, `Pariah.cpp` / `Twilight.cpp` bytes.
- **`FUN_00A59340`** favored-enemy damage multiplier, custom convention: `ecx` = attacker, `eax` = target (CombatUnit subobjects), returns float in `st0`. Vanilla: own hero spec `0x1C` (Forest Guardian) + attacker faction 4 + target in the hero's favored enemies → `1 + clamp(level × DefaultStats[+0x85C] + [+0x858], 0, 10)`, else 1.0. Only caller: `func_ComputeDamageMitigation` (`0x00A5A900`) at `0x00A5AE0C` (result multiplied into the damage).
- **Favored enemies**: `IHero` vtable `+0x25C` (`0x00B4CE20`, returns `[this+0x188]`; `IHero::favored_enemies()`), then its vtable `+0x0C` (creature id) → bool.
- **Creature of a combat unit**: `ICombatCreature::creature()` (`src/structs/Creature.h`). CombatUnit vtable `+0x70` `get_combat_stack` returns the combat stack interface `ICombatStack` (RTTI `NWorld::ICombatCreature`, vtable `0x00E4FE9C`, complete object `+0xA0`; null for heroes), whose slot `+0` returns the `ICreature*` (`type_id` at `+0x1C`, `count` at `+0x20`). All 35 slots are documented in `CombatStack_vtable`. Faction: `0x004BA910` (`get_creature_town`, creature data `+0x98`).
- **Spell damage mitigation** `func_ComputeSpellDamageMitigation` (`0x0097AF50`): `ebx` = defending side's `IHero`, `edi` = defending unit. The old Luck of the Barbarian block `0x0097B055`–`0x0097B0B2` used `luck > 0 ? 1 : 0` (`setg` at `0x0097B076`); `SkillEffectDisable.cpp` used to disable it with `EB` at `0x0097B066` (removed). `ModSpellProof.cpp` / `ModElementalResistance.cpp` hook later in the same function.

Hook sites to avoid: `0x004E66C2` is `PhoenixFeatherCape.cpp`. `0x008A4B5C` / `0x008A25ED` are `ModAttack.cpp` / `ModDefense.cpp`. `0x008A3F98`–`0x008A3FAF` is `ArtfsetPreserve.cpp` (Sylvan 6).
